# UI colour contrast

When you change colours, backgrounds, or chrome under `front/`:

1. Check contrast for text and icons against their background. Aim for WCAG AA (about 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text / UI chrome).
2. Prefer shared tokens from `design/tokens.css` (`--color-text`, `--color-bg`, `--color-accent`, `--color-on-accent`) over one-off hex pairs. Amvara navy/red only.
3. Glass / blur only on chrome over a known solid wash, never under body copy. If contrast fails, drop the glass.
4. Day and night tokens must both pass AA. Fix tokens before shipping.
